276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 182 0 R
/E (We trained two versions of FFLUNet on brain tumor MRI scans to segment three tumor regions: the necrotic core \(dead tissue\), edema \(swelling\), and enhancing tumor \(active cancer cells\).)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 182 0 R
/E (The standard FFLUNet learns from only the final output. The deep supervision version gets extra feedback signals from intermediate layers during training, forcing the network to build useful features at every scale, not just the last one.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
